# Git remote-writes on explicit order

Do not run git remote-write commands (`git push`, `git -C … push`, or any other remote-write subcommand) unless the user explicitly asked for that write. "Push", "open the PR", or "publish the branch" are enough.

Local git **read** commands may run without asking.

Completing implementation is not an implicit push. Vague ship-it language without a named target uses the Operator Gate.

When the user asked to push: warn before force-push to main/master.

## Worktrees must stay attached

When creating or managing a task worktree, the agent must check out and keep the worktree on its task branch. Never create or leave a task worktree in detached `HEAD` state, including via `git worktree add --detach`, unless the user explicitly asks for a detached worktree.
